# Manifest course waiver

Until 2026-11-16, an existing manifest course may break. A file-based lessons course (`$CFG->lessons`, no `manifest_id`) may not.

From 2026-11-02 on, the first time a conversation touches lessons, manifests, LTI content, or course settings, tell the user even if they just said manifest courses can break:

CodeRabbit's waiver expires 2026-11-16. After that it will flag existing manifest courses that regress. Extend the date, or let it expire?

Say that once in the conversation, then keep working. On or after 2026-11-16 the waiver is over. Do not move the date yourself. Ask whether manifest courses are now production, and delete this rule and the matching section in `AGENTS.md` and `.coderabbit.yaml` once the user decides.
